/-!
# The reduction of a formal spectrum

Let `S` be a scheme contained in a big fppf site `B`, let `A` be a weakly admissible
topological ring over `S` and let `𝔞 ⊆ A` be its ideal of topologically nilpotent elements.
Every weak ideal of definition of `A` consists of topologically nilpotent elements and is
therefore contained in `𝔞`; since one of them is open, so is `𝔞`, and `𝔞` is itself a weak
ideal of definition — the largest one. The quotient spectra of the weak ideals of definition
are ordered by reverse inclusion and their colimit is `Spf A`, so `Spec (A ⧸ 𝔞)` is the
terminal stage of that diagram. Moreover `𝔞` is a radical ideal, so `A ⧸ 𝔞` is reduced.

Consequently the stage morphism `Spec (A ⧸ 𝔞) ⟶ Spf A` exhibits `Spec (A ⧸ 𝔞)` as the
reduction of `Spf A`: it is a morphism from a reduced algebraic space, and it is representable
and a thickening because it is a stage of a presentation whose transition morphisms are
thickenings. A morphism to `Spf A` from a reduced algebraic space factors uniquely through it,
because a representable thickening is injective on sections, and over an étale cover of the
source by a reduced object of the site a factorization exists. In the notation of the source,
`Spf(A)_red = Spec (A ⧸ 𝔞)`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isReduction_formalSpectrum`: the stage of the formal spectrum
  at the ideal of topologically nilpotent elements is the reduction of the formal spectrum.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.relative_uliftYoneda_of_relative_sheafifiedYoneda`: a relative
  morphism property along the sheafified Yoneda embedding holds along the universe-lifted
  Yoneda embedding of presheaves.

## Implementation notes

The reduction is expressed through `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.IsReduction`, the predicate
naming the defining properties of the reduction of a formal algebraic space, rather than
through a construction: the conclusion is that the canonical morphism has those properties, so
no existence statement and no choice is involved.

Two universe-levels of representability occur. The presentation statements for a stage of an
affine formal algebraic space are relative to the sheafified Yoneda embedding, whereas the
properties of a morphism of formal algebraic spaces are relative to the universe-lifted Yoneda
embedding into presheaves, because a formal algebraic space is a sheaf of `Type (u + 1)`. On a
subcanonical site the two embeddings agree after composing with the inclusion of sheaves into
presheaves, and `relative_uliftYoneda_of_relative_sheafifiedYoneda` moves a relative property
across that identification: a represented base change computed in sheaves is computed in
presheaves, the inclusion of sheaves into presheaves preserving limits.

That every stage of the formal spectrum is representable and a relative thickening — the stage
form of Stacks 0AI9 — is derived from the colimit presentation of the formal spectrum, in the
shortest form that argument takes: the transition morphisms are thickenings because the image
of one weak ideal of definition is nilpotent modulo another, and the index of weak ideals of
definition is directed for reverse inclusion.

The unique factorization of a morphism from a reduced algebraic space is proved directly from
the two representability properties rather than from the factorization through a stage of an
affine formal algebraic space, which is available only for a quasi-compact source presented by
a presheaf of `Type u`. A representable thickening is injective on sections, since a lift of a
section splits the base change and a split closed immersion is an isomorphism; and a section of
the source pulled back to an étale cover of it by a reduced object of the site lifts, since the
base change of the thickening to a reduced object is an isomorphism. The sheaf condition on the
covering sieve generated by one surjective étale morphism then assembles the lifts, injectivity
making them compatible.

The two properties of the ideal of topologically nilpotent elements that the statement rests on
are Stacks 0AMW and are already available: it is a weak ideal of definition
(`TopologicalRing.isWeakIdealOfDefinition_topologicalNilradical`) and it is a radical ideal
(`TopologicalRing.topologicalNilradical_isRadical`), so `A ⧸ 𝔞` is reduced.

